  "measured": "2026-11-04",
  "method": "Cairn-only diagnostic companion to delete_single_key.py: the same exact 12,000-key 4 KiB pool and the same one-signed-DELETE-per-key client at bounded concurrency, plus /metrics scrapes one full 15 s store-metrics tick apart on both sides of the scored delete window. Arms are fresh single-node stores under the same strict settings the official comparison pins (synchronous=full, one shard, linger 0). One exclusive host-wide benchmark lock was held for each batch; no other benchmark ran concurrently. Stage means come from the writer's bounded per-stage sample rings (admission/queue/begin/apply/commit/checkpoint); commit and batch means come from the per-commit ring, which holds every commit of an arm. control-c16-final re-ran the script with the sampler restricted to the scored window on a busy host; control-c16-final2 is the final script on a quiet host and is also the arm that carries the DELETE-labelled request histogram (12,000 requests, 9.301 ms mean handler time, which is the queue plus apply plus the commit barrier). Across the session the same control binary measured 1,176-1,613 obj/s at c16 while the commit share stayed 77-84%, so only within-batch comparisons are drawn.",
